# Extractions are tracked here; raw cartridge images are not.
# Anyone with the cart can regenerate these, and git handles a 64MB blob badly.
#
# Savestates follow the same rule, applied by cost rather than by extension. Only the
# ones that took real manual work and that no script recreates are tracked, gzipped, in
# save_states/ -- currently three. Anything boot_verified.py can regenerate in a couple
# of minutes is deliberately absent, and save_states/INDEX.md lists what was left out
# and how to remake it. A raw .mln is 18.4MB and gzips to ~1.9MB, so tracking the whole
# set would have cost 184MB to store states a script rebuilds on demand.
*.nds
*.sav
*.dsv

# Local scratch
.DS_Store
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Regenerable analysis caches (not artifacts -- rebuild instead of tracking)
analysis/strings_cache/
